// Literal, zero-hole frame for "Sacrifice this permanent" — the general
// "Sacrifice this <TYPE>" family has no frame: no hole models "this <the
// invoking card's own type>", only this one literal wording.
//
// The `~` self-reference sigil is a rejected parameterized alternative:
// `~` resolves structurally to `NounPhrase::ThisCard`
// (`crates/deckmaste_english/src/syntax/phrase.rs`), which renders as the
// card's own printed name, never a type-generic demonstrative. This macro
// is invoked live by
// `plugins/builtin/tokens/{Clue,Gold,Treasure,Food,Blood}.ron`, whose
// checked-in `template:` renders "Sacrifice this artifact" — a `~`-framed
// authoring would flip that to "Sacrifice Clue"/"Sacrifice Gold"/etc.
(
    name: "SacrificeThis",
    template: "Sacrifice this permanent",
    kinds: [CostComponent],
    frames: ["Sacrifice this permanent"],
    body: Do(Sacrifice(You, This)),
)
